{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Network and Database Administrators"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about the features of network and database administrators jobs."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts. Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understand important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.  Exchange simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Have You Got? And, Do You Have?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use both <span class=\"strong\">Have you got</span> and <span class=\"strong\">Do you have</span> structures to ask about possession. The difference is that <span class=\"strong\">Have you got </span>is more informal than <span class=\"strong\">Do you have</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"strong\">Do you have?</span><br><br>  This interrogative structure is based on the simple present tense. That's why you use the auxiliary verbs Do/Does depending on the person you are talking about. This structure is the most commonly used in the United States, while <span class=\"strong\">have you got </span>is the most commonly used in the United Kingdom in informal contexts. <br><br>  You can answer to these questions by using the auxiliary verb instead of using the whole complement; it's commonly known as a short answer.<br><br>  Structure:<br> <div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"strong\">Do/Does</span> + subject + <span class=\"strong\">have</span> + complement + <span class=\"strong\">?</span> </div> Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Do</span> you <span class=\"strong\">have</span> a laptop<span class=\"strong\">?</span></span><br><br> Long answers: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> Yes, I <span class=\"strong\">have</span> a laptop.<br> No, I <span class=\"strong\">don't</span> have a laptop.</span><br><br> Short answers: <br><span class=\"italic\"> Yes, I <span class=\"strong\">do</span>.<br> No, I <span class=\"strong\">don't</span>.</span><br><br>   <span class=\"strong\">Have you got?</span><br><br>  This interrogative structure use the verb <span class=\"strong\">Have</span> as an auxiliary and the verb <span class=\"strong\">Got</span> with a present connotation.<br>  <div class=\"center_text\">  <span class=\"strong\">Have/Has</span> + subject + <span class=\"strong\">got</span> + complement +?</div><br> Example:<br>  <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Have</span> you <span class=\"strong\">got</span> a laptop?<br> Yes, I <span class=\"strong\">have</span>.<br> No, I <span class=\"strong\">haven't</span>.<br><br> </span> Look at the examples in the table:\t "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">DO YOU HAVE? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> HAVE YOU GOT?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u2022\\t<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Do</span>   they <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have</span>   a database administrator<span class=\\\"strong\\\">?</span>   <br /><br />  Yes, they <span class=\\\"strong\\\">do</span>.  <br /> No, they <span class=\\\"strong\\\">don't</span>  .\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \u2022\\t<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Have</span> they <span class=\\\"strong\\\">got</span> a database administrator<span class=\\\"strong\\\">?</span><br /><br />  Yes, they <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have</span>.<br /> No, they <span class=\\\"strong\\\">haven't</span>.<br /><br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \u2022\\t<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Does</span> Christina <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have</span> a new IT position<span class=\\\"strong\\\">?</span><br /><br />  Yes, she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">does</span>.<br /> No, she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">doesn't</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \u2022\\t<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Has</span> Christina <span class=\\\"strong\\\">got</span> a new IT position<span class=\\\"strong\\\">?</span><br /><br />  Yes, she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has</span>.<br /> No, she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hasn't</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you have the same training?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you have enough experience in databases?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you got any special training for this?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you got other tasks?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Collocations Related to Computers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Collocations are some specific words that need to be together because they form the appropriate and natural expressions in natural English. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is very important for English learners to know collocations; the usage of wrong words could foment a misunderstanding.<br><br>In the following chart you can check some common collocations related to computers:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">COMPUTER + NOUN</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> VERB + COMPUTER </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Computer network\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Run a/the computer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Computer program\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use a/the computer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Computer system\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Switch on the computer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Computer equipment\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Switch off the computer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Computer hardware\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Log onto a/the computer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Computer software\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Boot up the  computer\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I set up and test storage in computer systems."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I design recovery and back-up computer programs."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "set up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to install"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I set up and test storage in computer systems."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "recovery"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of reestablishing something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example"